                                        "entry_id": "cd7cf48b-e737-3bc1-8774-a76cdbbc50c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any small rodent of the genus Mus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19dc8bfc-c7fe-4df6-b125-a21f9849a72c",
                                                "sense_id": "24504261-00e3-3ff4-ae25-ba0f6a5cacb3",
                                                "text": "At twilight in the summer there is never anybody to fear—man, woman, or cat—in the chambers and at that hour the mice come out. They do not eat parchment or foolscap or red tape, but they eat the luncheon crumbs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06cfc9c5-247e-453f-b1a4-26a195a903ea",
                                                "sense_id": "24504261-00e3-3ff4-ae25-ba0f6a5cacb3",
                                                "text": "A person smeared with the excrement of a mouse was rendered impotent, according to Pliny the Elder."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "347a2d49-3f48-4fe8-bbf5-b44fee83b551",
                                                "sense_id": "24504261-00e3-3ff4-ae25-ba0f6a5cacb3",
                                                "text": "In molecular biologist David Sinclair’s lab at Harvard Medical School, old mice are growing young again. […] After injecting the virus into the eye, the pluripotent genes were then switched on by feeding the mouse an antibiotic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f449e6a5-20d7-39a6-9e71-c75fc7d956a7",
                                        "entry_id": "cd7cf48b-e737-3bc1-8774-a76cdbbc50c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of the many small rodent and marsupial species resembling mice, typically having a small body, dark fur, long tail, and nocturnal sleeping pattern compared to rats."
                                        ],
